  ['COPY 03', 'GlowHaus Beauty Studio', `Tired of dull, difficult-to-manage hair?<br><br>It’s frustrating when your hair looks dry, flat, or unstyled no matter how much effort you put in. You spend time getting ready but still don’t feel confident with your look.<br><br>Meet GlowHaus Beauty Studio. Our Signature Hair Refresh includes a professional haircut and blowout to give you polished, fresh, and easy-to-style hair.<br><br>“I left feeling refreshed, confident, and ready for the week.” – Sample Client Testimonial<br><br>Click below to book your Signature Hair Refresh for only $49 today!<br>👉 Book Your Appointment<br>[Insert Booking Link]`],
  ['COPY 04', 'GlowHaus Beauty Studio', `Pagod ka na ba sa buhok na laging dry, dull, at mahirap i-style?<br><br>Nakaka-frustrate kapag kahit anong ayos mo, hindi pa rin fresh tingnan ang hair mo. Nauubos ang oras mo sa pag-prepare pero hindi ka pa rin confident sa final look.<br><br>Meet GlowHaus Beauty Studio. Sa aming Signature Hair Refresh, makakakuha ka ng professional haircut and blowout para mas polished, fresh, at madaling ayusin ang buhok mo.<br><br>“After my appointment, mas fresh at confident na ang feeling ko.” – Sample Client Testimonial<br><br>Book your beauty refresh for only $49 today!<br>👉 Book Your Appointment<br>[Insert Booking Link]`],
  ['COPY 05', 'Brew & Bloom Café', `Tired of the same ordinary coffee every morning?<br><br>It’s disappointing when your coffee feels plain, rushed, and forgettable. You deserve a drink that makes your morning feel a little warmer and more enjoyable.<br><br>Meet Brew & Bloom Café’s Honey Oat Latte—made with smooth espresso, creamy oat milk, and a touch of honey for a comforting sweetness in every sip.<br><br>“My new favorite latte—smooth, creamy, and just the right amount of sweet.” – Sample Customer Testimonial<br><br>Click below to try the Honey Oat Latte for only $6.50 today!<br>👉 Drop By Today<br>[Insert Café Location or Link]`],
  ['COPY 06', 'Brew & Bloom Café', `Nagsasawa ka na ba sa ordinary coffee na pare-pareho ang lasa?<br><br>Nakaka-disappoint kapag ang morning coffee mo ay plain, rushed, at walang special feeling. Minsan, kailangan mo lang ng comforting drink para mas maging enjoyable ang araw mo.<br><br>Try Brew & Bloom Café’s Honey Oat Latte—made with smooth espresso, creamy oat milk, at tamang sweetness ng honey sa bawat sip.<br><br>“Bagong favorite latte ko—creamy, smooth, at sakto lang ang tamis.” – Sample Customer Testimonial<br><br>Try the Honey Oat Latte for only $6.50 today!<br>👉 Drop By Today<br>123 Garden Lane | Open daily, 7 AM–8 PM`],
  ['COPY 07', 'LearnLab Academy', `Struggling to speak English with confidence?<br><br>It’s frustrating when you know what you want to say but hesitate because of grammar mistakes or limited vocabulary. You miss opportunities to communicate, participate, and express yourself clearly.<br><br>Meet LearnLab Academy. Our practical English lessons help you learn useful vocabulary, practice real conversations, and build confidence step by step.<br><br>“LearnLab helped me feel more comfortable speaking English every day.” – Sample Student Testimonial<br><br>Click below to enroll in the next class with Ms. Andrea Cruz!<br>👉 Start Learning Today<br>[Insert Enrollment Link]`],
  ['COPY 08', 'LearnLab Academy', `Nahihirapan ka bang magsalita ng English nang confident?<br><br>Nakaka-frustrate kapag alam mo naman ang gusto mong sabihin pero naghe-hesitate ka dahil sa grammar mistakes o kulang sa vocabulary. Nawawala ang chance mong makapag-express nang maayos at makipag-communicate confidently.<br><br>Meet LearnLab Academy. Matututo ka ng practical English, useful phrases, at real conversation skills para unti-unti kang maging mas confident sa pagsasalita.<br><br>“Mas naging comfortable akong magsalita ng English dahil sa LearnLab.” – Sample Student Testimonial<br><br>Enroll sa next class with Ms. Andrea Cruz!<br>👉 Start Learning Today<br>[Insert Enrollment Link]`],
  ['COPY 09', 'Soléa Fashion Co.', `Struggling to create stylish outfits every day?<br><br>It’s frustrating to have a full closet but still feel like you have nothing to wear. Choosing outfits takes time, and many pieces don’t work well together.<br><br>Meet Soléa Fashion Co.’s The Everyday Edit—a collection of neutral, timeless pieces designed to mix, match, and create effortless everyday looks.<br><br>“These pieces made getting dressed easier and more stylish.” – Sample Customer Testimonial<br><br>Click below to discover the new collection, with pieces from $42–$89.<br>👉 Shop the Collection<br>[Insert Shop Link]`],
  ['COPY 10', 'Soléa Fashion Co.', `Nahihirapan ka bang mag-isip ng stylish outfit araw-araw?<br><br>Nakaka-frustrate kapag puno ang closet mo pero feeling mo wala ka pa ring maisuot. Matagal kang pumipili ng outfit, pero hindi nagtutugma ang mga pieces.<br><br>Meet The Everyday Edit by Soléa Fashion Co.—neutral and timeless pieces na madaling i-mix and match para makagawa ka ng effortless everyday looks.<br><br>“Mas naging madali at stylish ang pag-dress up ko dahil sa collection na ito.” – Sample Customer Testimonial<br><br>Discover the new collection, with pieces from $42–$89.<br>👉 Shop the Collection<br>[Insert Shop Link]`]
].forEach(function (item) {
  const label = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('span')).find(function (candidate) {
    return candidate.textContent.trim().toUpperCase() === item[0];
  });
  const card = label ? label.closest('.rounded-xl') : null;
  if (!card) return;
  card.classList.add('group', 'relative', 'overflow-hidden', 'transition-all', 'duration-200');
  card.innerHTML = `<div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-2"><span class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-primary">${item[0]}</span><button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="copy-expand-button shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded bg-surface-container-highest px-2 py-1 text-[10px] font-label-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary transition-colors duration-200 hover:bg-primary hover:text-on-primary focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary/40"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[14px] leading-none">open_in_full</span><span>Expand</span></button></div><p class="font-label-sm text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mt-3">${item[1]}</p><p class="copy-preview font-body-sm text-[11px] text-on-surface-variant mt-2 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">${item[2]}</p>`;
  const button = card.querySelector('.copy-expand-button');
  const preview = card.querySelector('.copy-preview');
  const icon = button.querySelector('.material-symbols-outlined');
  const buttonLabel = button.querySelector('span:last-child');
  button.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
    event.stopPropagation();
    const expanded = card.classList.toggle('copy-card-expanded');
    preview.classList.toggle('line-clamp-3', !expanded);
    icon.textContent = expanded ? 'close_fullscreen' : 'open_in_full';
    buttonLabel.textContent = expanded ? 'Minimize' : 'Expand';
    button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(expanded));
  });
});
document.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
  document.querySelectorAll('.copy-card-expanded').forEach(function (card) {
    if (card.contains(event.target)) return;
    card.classList.remove('copy-card-expanded');
    const preview = card.querySelector('.copy-preview');
    const button = card.querySelector('.copy-expand-button');
    const icon = button ? button.querySelector('.material-symbols-outlined') : null;
    const buttonLabel = button ? button.querySelector('span:last-child') : null;
    if (preview) preview.classList.add('line-clamp-3');
    if (button) {
      if (icon) icon.textContent = 'open_in_full';
      if (buttonLabel) buttonLabel.textContent = 'Expand';
      button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    }
  });
});
const copywritingHeading = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('h4')).find(function (heading) {
  return heading.textContent.trim() === 'Copywriting samples';
});
if (copywritingHeading) {
  const copyHeader = copywritingHeading.closest('.flex');
  const oldGrid = copyHeader ? copyHeader.nextElementSibling : null;
  if (copyHeader && oldGrid) {
    copyHeader.id = 'copywriting-samples';
    const copyDescription = copyHeader.querySelector('p');
    if (copyDescription) copyDescription.textContent = 'Brand-focused ad copy, email campaigns, practical tips, and short-form video scripts created for different audiences and content goals.';
    const copyCount = copyHeader.querySelector('span:last-child');
    if (copyCount) copyCount.textContent = '20 samples';
    oldGrid.className = 'copywriting-table-scroll';
    oldGrid.innerHTML = `<div class="copywriting-table"><div class="copywriting-header"><div class="copywriting-header-cell">Brand</div><div class="copywriting-header-cell">Ad Copy</div><div class="copywriting-header-cell">Email</div><div class="copywriting-header-cell">Tips</div><div class="copywriting-header-cell">Short Video Scripts</div></div><div class="copywriting-body"></div></div>`;
    const copyRows = [
      ['PrimeNest Realty', [`<strong>Kung 15 years mo babayaran, hindi pwedeng “maganda naman sa brochure” lang ang basis mo.</strong><br><br>Real talk, ang hirap bumili ng property kapag nasa abroad ka. You’re working long shifts, nagpapadala sa pamilya, tapos ang makikita mo lang minsan is polished renders, magandang lobby, and an agent saying, “Ma’am, last few units na po.”<br><br>Pero wait—kamusta ang drainage? May signs ba ng water pooling? Anong klaseng partitions ang ginamit? Maayos ba ang concrete finishing? Ano ang actual progress ng project versus sa promised timeline?<br><br>These are the boring questions na hindi aesthetic sa virtual tour, pero sila yung pwedeng makaapekto sa comfort, maintenance, resale value, at peace of mind mo years from now.<br><br>At PrimeNest Realty, we’d rather show you the details—including the things na hindi perfect—than pressure you into a reservation you’re not ready for.<br><br>Because after everything you sacrificed abroad, your property should feel like security… not another source of stress.<br><br>May project kang tinitingnan pero hindi mo ma-check personally? Send us the details. We can help you look at it with a more practical set of eyes. 🏠`, `<strong>Preheader:</strong> If the end goal is a home in the Philippines, don’t let one rushed decision ruin years of sacrifice.<br><br>May moment yata ang bawat OFW na ganito.<br><br>End of shift.<br>Pagod na pagod ka.<br>Tapos bubuksan mo ’yung family group chat.<br><br>May bagong picture ng anak mo.<br>Birthday na hindi mo napuntahan.<br>Dinner na sana kasama ka.<br><br>And you remind yourself:<br><br><strong>“Para sa future namin ’to.”</strong><br><br>For a lot of Filipinos abroad, that future eventually looks like one thing: a home you can finally call yours.<br><br>Kaya ang sakit isipin na after years of sacrifice, one rushed property decision can lock you into payments for the next 10 or 15 years.<br><br>Especially when you’re thousands of kilometers away and all you have is a brochure, a rendering, and an agent saying: “Maganda po ’yan, ma’am.”<br><br>Sorry, pero hindi sapat ang “maganda.”<br><br>We want to know what you’re actually buying.<br><br>So for <strong>48 hours only</strong>, PrimeNest Realty is running an <strong>OFW Buyer Assurance Flash Offer</strong> on select properties.<br><br>Qualifying reservations can get a <strong>₱30,000 credit toward the property purchase</strong>.<br><br>But more importantly, we’re making it easier for you to verify before you commit.<br><br>You can request a <strong>live virtual walkthrough</strong> of the property or project.<br>Ask about the drainage.<br>Ask about wall construction.<br>Ask about finishes.<br>Ask about actual site progress.<br><br>We’ll also provide the available <strong>specifications, payment details, and project information</strong> so you can review them from abroad instead of relying on a hard-sell conversation.<br><br>For qualifying buyers, we’ll include a <strong>documented pre-turnover snagging walkthrough</strong> to help identify visible issues before acceptance.<br><br>Because the goal isn’t just to say: “May property na ako.”<br><br>The goal is to come home someday and feel:<br><br><strong>“Worth it lahat.”</strong><br><br><strong>[See the eligible PrimeNest properties and secure the 48-hour buyer offer here]</strong><br><br>Look through the details.<br>Ask the uncomfortable questions.<br>Then make the decision that makes sense for you and your family.<br><br>— PrimeNest Realty<br><br><strong>P.S.</strong> Promo applies only to qualifying units and is subject to availability and full terms. We’d rather show you the numbers and property details upfront than surprise you later.`, `Working abroad already takes so much from you, so the last thing you need is to spend 15 years paying for a property you never properly checked. And honestly, bhie, a nice virtual tour can hide a lot.<br><br><strong>5 tips to avoid buying a property you’ll regret from abroad</strong><br><br><strong>1. Ask for actual site videos:</strong> Request raw walkthroughs of the unit, hallways, drainage, parking, and surrounding area—not just edited reels.<br><br><strong>2. Check the boring details:</strong> Ask about wall thickness, waterproofing, drainage slope, ventilation, and actual materials used.<br><br><strong>3. Verify the developer:</strong> Look beyond ads—check completed projects, turnover history, reviews, and documented delays.<br><br><strong>4. Read the payment terms twice:</strong> Know the total contract price, fees, penalties, turnover costs, and what happens if construction gets delayed.<br><br><strong>5. Get a second set of eyes:</strong> Have a trusted person, engineer, or independent inspector check the property before you commit.<br><br>Because when you’re buying from thousands of kilometers away, trust is good—but proof is better.<br><br>Save this before your next virtual property viewing.`, `0–3s — Handheld selfie shot, casual video-call vibe. Quick cut to a property render on a laptop.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> POV: you’re abroad and about to pay for a property for the next 15 years… without seeing it in person.<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Okay, this is probably the scariest part about buying property while you’re abroad.”<br><br>3–7s — Cut from a polished render to actual construction clips.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> a nice render doesn’t always mean a good build<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Because honestly, a nice render isn’t enough. I wanna see the actual site.”<br><br>7–13s — Close-ups of drainage, walls, concrete finish, windows, and construction progress.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> check the drainage. walls. finishing. progress.<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Show me the drainage, the walls, the finishing, the actual construction progress. Like… everything.”<br><br>13–19s — Scroll through project documents, walkthrough videos, and progress updates.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> get the receipts before you reserve<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Before you reserve anything, you should have documents, updated walkthroughs, and clear answers. Not just ‘this is the last unit.’”<br><br>19–25s — Back to selfie cam with a subtle PrimeNest logo.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> less pressure. more due diligence.<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “That’s how we want PrimeNest to work. No pressure. Just helping you understand what you’re actually paying for.”<br><br>25–28s — Show a simple property checklist on a phone.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> DM “CHECKLIST”<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “If you’re buying from abroad, message us ‘CHECKLIST.’ We’ll send you what to verify before paying anything.”`]],
      ['GlowHaus Beauty Studio', [`<strong>Bhie, masyado kang maganda para magtiis sa buhok na “pwede na.” 😭</strong><br><br>Like… nag-save ka ng 47 hair inspo sa Pinterest, may buong TikTok folder ka ng dream looks, tapos paglabas mo ng salon parang <em>“ate, hindi po ito yung nasa reference…”</em> UBEH??? Jail.<br><br>At GlowHaus Beauty Studio, hindi ka namin bibigyan ng outdated na interpretation ng peg mo. We get the assignment: modern, flattering, camera-ready, at bagay sa <strong>ikaw</strong>—hindi basta trend na pinilit sa buhok mo.<br><br>Because your hair should be serving sa mirror, sa front cam, at especially sa random 0.5 photos na hindi mo napaghandaan. Period.<br><br>May peg ka na matagal nang naka-save? Send mo sa DM. Tingnan natin kung paano natin siya gagawing bagay sa’yo. ✨`, `<strong>Preheader:</strong> 30% OFF GlowHaus hair services for 24 hours. Your camera roll deserves better.<br><br>Okay, imagine this.<br><br>The outfit? Ate.<br>Makeup? Face card undefeated.<br>Lighting? Giving Pinterest board.<br><br>Then you open the front cam and your hair is just… there.<br><br>Bestie. Be serious.<br><br>You are way too cute to be fighting for your life with a hairstyle that stopped trending three TikTok audios ago.<br><br>So GlowHaus is doing something a little reckless for the next 24 hours:<br><br><strong>30% OFF ALL HAIR SERVICES.</strong><br><br>Yes. Thirty percent.<br><br>Go for the glossy blowout.<br>Get the face-framing layers.<br>Finally book the color refresh you’ve had sitting in your Pinterest saves for six months.<br><br>And no, we’re not giving you the “Tita said this looks good” treatment.<br><br>We’re talking soft, flattering, camera-ready hair that actually understands the assignment.<br><br>But here’s the catch:<br><br>This is a <strong>24-hour flash sale</strong>, and once the available appointments are taken, that’s it.<br><br>No “sayang, I was about to book.”<br>No dramatic messages tomorrow.<br>You had your chance, gorgeous.<br><br><strong>[Click here to claim 30% OFF and secure your GlowHaus slot]</strong><br><br>Come in cute.<br>Leave looking like your next Reel accidentally became your profile picture.<br><br>— GlowHaus Beauty Studio<br><br><strong>P.S.</strong> Your saved hairstyle inspo deserves to leave the Pinterest board eventually. This is the sign.`, `<strong>Your haircut is not “low maintenance” just because the TikTok girl said hers is.</strong><br><br>Bhie, she may have extensions, a Dyson, three products, and 40 minutes every morning—we need context.<br><br><strong>5 tips to choose a hairstyle you can actually maintain</strong><br><br><strong>1. Count your styling minutes:</strong> Pick a cut that fits your real morning routine.<br><strong>2. Factor in humidity:</strong> Manila weather has opinions too, babe.<br><strong>3. Consider your natural texture:</strong> A cut should work even before the flat iron enters the chat.<br><strong>4. Ask how it grows out:</strong> Cute today and awkward in three weeks? No thank you.<br><strong>5. Choose realistic upkeep:</strong> The best hairstyle is one you can still serve on a random Tuesday.<br><br>Be honest: are you a 30-minute blowout girlie or a “suklay then go” girlie?<br><br><strong>CTA:</strong> Keep this in mind bago ka mag-decide sa next hair transformation mo.`, `<strong>The Viral Haircut Trap</strong><br><br><strong>0–3s</strong> — Client scrolling wolf cuts and butterfly cuts on TikTok.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> POV: you got the viral haircut… now you hate styling it<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Okay bhie, nobody warned you about this part.”<br><br><strong>3–7s</strong> — Hair shown naturally before styling.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> viral doesn’t mean low-maintenance<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “That cute haircut? She still needs styling.”<br><br><strong>7–12s</strong> — Stylist shows the layers and explains placement.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> ask how it looks WITHOUT heat<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Before you commit, ask how it behaves on your natural hair.”<br><br><strong>12–17s</strong> — Quick split showing styled versus natural finish.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> cute both ways &gt; cute for 20 mins<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Because we need hair that survives real life.”<br><br><strong>17–22s</strong> — Client leaves the salon with effortless movement.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> be realistic, babe<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Your morning routine matters.”<br><br><strong>Caption:</strong> That viral cut might be serving on TikTok because she spent 30 minutes styling it before filming. Meanwhile ikaw, five minutes lang and aalis ka na. Choose a cut that matches your real routine. Ask how it grows out, how it looks air-dried, and how much styling it actually needs.`] ],
      ['Brew & Bloom Café', [`<strong>Some mornings deserve flowers, good coffee, and absolutely no unnecessary noise.</strong><br><br>There are days when you don’t need another packed schedule. You just need a quiet corner, the scent of fresh blooms, and a cup of coffee made with a little more care.<br><br>That’s the kind of pause we love creating at Brew & Bloom Café.<br><br>Nothing too loud. Nothing too rushed. Just a calm space where conversations can linger, mornings can move slowly, and your coffee actually tastes the way it should.<br><br>Because peace is a luxury too—and sometimes, it looks like fresh flowers beside your cup and an afternoon with nowhere else to be. 🌷<br><br>Come by when the city feels a little too much.`, `<strong>Preheader:</strong> Consider this your invitation to slow down—plus a little something from us on your first visit.<br><br>You know that kind of Saturday morning?<br>No alarm.<br>No Teams notifications.<br>No one asking you for “just one quick thing.”<br>You finally have nowhere urgent to be.<br><br>So naturally, you want coffee.<br>Not coffee while standing in a 20-minute line.<br>Not coffee in a room so loud you can hear four different conversations and somebody’s TikTok playing from across the table.<br>And definitely not an espresso that tastes like it has unresolved anger issues.<br><br>Sometimes, you just want to sit somewhere beautiful…<br>take a proper sip…<br>and hear yourself think.<br><br>That’s exactly why we created <strong>Brew & Bloom Café.</strong><br><br>Think artisanal coffee made with care.<br>Fresh, quality ingredients.<br>Greenery, soft floral touches, and a space designed for slow mornings, quiet catch-ups, and the occasional <em>“I’m unavailable today, thank you very much”</em> moment.<br><br>And since you’ve just joined our little corner of calm, we’d love to welcome you properly.<br><br>For your <strong>first visit within the next 14 days</strong>, order any <strong>Signature Coffee</strong> and your choice of one <strong>house-made pastry is on us.</strong><br><br>No complicated points.<br>No five-step membership ritual.<br>Just something lovely to enjoy with your coffee.<br><br><strong>[Click here to claim your Brew & Bloom Welcome Ritual and plan your first visit]</strong><br><br>Come alone with a book.<br>Bring the friend you’ve been saying <em>“we need to catch up”</em> to for three months.<br>Or simply give yourself one peaceful hour where nobody needs anything from you.<br><br>Your table is waiting.<br><br>Warmly,<br><strong>Brew & Bloom Café</strong><br><br><strong>P.S.</strong> Your complimentary pastry is available with any Signature Coffee on your first visit within 14 days of subscribing, subject to availability. And yes—taking your sweet time is highly encouraged.`, `You know when you finally get a free morning, sit down for coffee, and somehow the café is louder than your entire work week? Like… I came here to relax, not to fight for a table and drink burnt espresso.<br><br><strong>5 tips to make your coffee date actually feel relaxing</strong><br><br><strong>1. Pick a place you can actually talk:</strong> If you’re shouting across the table, the vibe is already gone.<br><br><strong>2. Order coffee that tastes balanced:</strong> Good espresso shouldn’t taste burned or covered up with syrup.<br><br><strong>3. Choose somewhere you want to stay:</strong> Comfortable seats, greenery, and a calm setup make such a difference.<br><br><strong>4. Don’t rush the whole thing:</strong> Give yourself time to sit, catch up, and actually enjoy your drink.<br><br><strong>5. Make it feel like a ritual:</strong> Your coffee break should feel like a reset, not another task on your list.<br><br>And honestly, sometimes you just need one quiet morning, good coffee, and your favorite person to talk to.<br><br>Save this for your next slow weekend catch-up.`, `<strong>0–3s</strong> — Handheld selfie entering the café. Quick cut to a quiet corner, flowers on the table, and coffee being poured.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> POV: you finally found a café that doesn’t stress you out<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Wait… why is it actually peaceful in here?”<br><br><strong>3–7s</strong> — Slow pan of greenery, soft seating, natural light, pastries, and no visible crowd chaos.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> no shouting. no crazy lines. no burnt coffee.<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Like, no loud crowd, no fighting for a table, and the coffee doesn’t taste burnt.”<br><br><strong>7–12s</strong> — Close-up of espresso pulling, milk texture, fresh flowers, and ingredients being prepared.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> good coffee + actual calm<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “They use proper ingredients, the coffee’s smooth, and somehow the whole place just feels… expensive but cozy.”<br><br><strong>12–18s</strong> — Two friends casually chatting and laughing over coffee.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> this is the kind of place you stay too long<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “You come for one coffee and suddenly it’s been two hours because no one’s rushing you.”<br><br><strong>18–24s</strong> — Hero shot of coffee beside flowers, a book, sunglasses, or handbag.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> Brew & Bloom Café<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Honestly, this is my kind of weekend reset.”<br><br><strong>24–27s</strong> — Selfie shot with the drink in hand and a small smile to camera.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> save this for your next slow morning<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Save this for your next coffee date.”`]],
      ['LearnLab Academy', [`<strong>Myth: Kailangan perfect ang grammar mo bago ka maging confident mag-English. Nope.</strong><br><br>Actually, ito yung dahilan kung bakit maraming matatalino at magagaling na students at young professionals ang biglang natahimik kapag kailangan nang magsalita.<br><br>Alam mo naman yung gusto mong sabihin. Kaya mong isulat nang maayos. Pero habang nagsasalita ka, sabay-sabay pumapasok sa utak mo: <em>“Tama ba grammar ko? Pangit ba pronunciation ko? Baka isipin nilang feeling smart ako?”</em><br><br>Ayun. Naunahan ka na ng overthinking bago mo pa matapos yung sentence.<br><br>Here’s the thing: conversational fluency isn’t built by being corrected every three seconds. You improve by actually speaking, making small mistakes, learning from them, and realizing na hindi pala katapusan ng mundo kapag hindi perfect ang isang sentence.<br><br>That’s why at LearnLab Academy, the goal isn’t to embarrass you into becoming “better.” We create a space where you can practice without feeling judged—because confidence grows when you feel safe enough to use your voice.<br><br>So kung magaling ka sa written English pero biglang <em>loading…</em> kapag ikaw na ang magsasalita, hindi ka nag-iisa. 😅<br><br>Send us a message if you want to practice English without feeling like may grammar police na nakaabang sa bawat sentence mo.`, `<strong>Preheader:</strong> 48 hours only: 40% OFF LearnLab’s Speak Without Fear Program + a bonus live practice session.<br><br>May tanong ang interviewer:<br><strong>“Tell me about yourself.”</strong><br><br>Easy.<br>You’ve answered this in your head approximately 47 times.<br>Perfect grammar.<br>Complete sentences.<br>May introduction, body, conclusion pa yata.<br><br>Pero nung actual interview na?<br>“Hi… yes… so… basically… I am…”<br><br>Tapos biglang nag-leave ang English vocabulary mo sa katawan mo.<br><br>Familiar?<br><br>Here’s the thing:<br><strong>Hindi ibig sabihin na mahina ka sa English.</strong><br><br>Sometimes, you know exactly what you want to say.<br>Pero dahil iniisip mo kung tama ba ang grammar mo…<br>kung pangit ba pronunciation mo…<br>kung baka isipin nilang “feeling smart” ka…<br><br>Your brain becomes so busy avoiding mistakes that speaking naturally becomes almost impossible.<br><br>And unfortunately, the usual solution is:<br>“Speak more confidently!”<br><br>Wow.<br>Thank you.<br>Very helpful.<br><br>At LearnLab Academy, we practice communication differently.<br><br>You’re allowed to pause.<br>You’re allowed to say something imperfectly.<br>You’re allowed to try again without someone making you feel like every grammatical error is a national emergency.<br><br>Because conversational confidence is built through <strong>safe, repeated practice</strong>—not embarrassment.<br><br>And for the next <strong>48 hours</strong>, we’re making it easier to start.<br><br>Get <strong>40% OFF our Speak Without Fear Program</strong> when you enroll during the flash sale.<br><br>You’ll practice real-life English for situations like:<br>Job interviews.<br>Presentations.<br>Meetings.<br>Networking.<br>Class discussions.<br><br>And those terrifying moments when someone suddenly says,<br><strong>“Ikaw naman. What do you think?”</strong><br><br>Plus, flash-sale enrollees get a <strong>FREE Live Confidence Practice Session</strong> where you can practice speaking in a supportive environment before using those skills in the real world.<br><br>No ridicule.<br>No “wrong!” every five seconds.<br>No expectation na dapat perfect ka agad.<br><br>Just practice, useful feedback, and actual conversations.<br><br><strong>[Click here to get 40% OFF and reserve your Speak Without Fear slot]</strong><br><br>You already know more English than you think.<br>Now let’s make it easier for you to actually <strong>use it when it counts.</strong><br><br>— LearnLab Academy<br><br><strong>P.S.</strong> The 40% flash-sale rate and bonus live session disappear after 48 hours. If “I’ll practice when I’m more confident” has been the plan for months… baka baliktad. Practice first. Confidence follows.`, `Just because you make grammar mistakes when speaking doesn’t mean you’re bad at English. Sometimes you freeze because you’re trying so hard to sound perfect that you forget to just talk.<br><br><strong>5 tips to speak English with more confidence without overthinking every word</strong><br><br><strong>1. Stop translating everything:</strong> Try thinking in simple English phrases instead of building the whole sentence in your head first.<br><br><strong>2. Choose clarity over perfection:</strong> Being understood matters more than getting every sentence completely right.<br><br><strong>3. Practice out loud:</strong> Reading helps, but speaking confidence only grows when you actually speak.<br><br><strong>4. Let small mistakes go:</strong> One wrong word doesn’t mean you need to restart the whole sentence.<br><br><strong>5. Practice somewhere safe:</strong> You improve faster when you’re not scared of being judged or corrected every few seconds.<br><br>You’re allowed to sound imperfect while you’re learning. That’s literally part of becoming fluent.<br><br>Save this for the next time you start overthinking before you speak.`, `<strong>0–3s</strong> — Student looking at the camera, clearly knowing the answer but hesitating to speak in a natural classroom or Zoom setup.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> POV: your English is good… until someone says “okay, you go first.”<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Quick myth: you’re probably not bad at English.”<br><br><strong>3–7s</strong> — Fast cut from a perfect written essay on a laptop to the student freezing during a conversation.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> the problem isn’t your grammar<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “You can write it. You understand it. But when it’s time to speak? Blank.”<br><br><strong>7–12s</strong> — Student makes a small mistake and pauses while the teacher listens calmly without interrupting.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> constant correction can make you speak LESS<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “Because if someone corrects every tiny mistake while you’re talking, your brain starts focusing on fear instead of conversation.”<br><br><strong>12–18s</strong> — Small-group roleplay with introductions, a job interview, and casual conversation. Everyone is relaxed and smiling.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> practice first. polish after.<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “At LearnLab, we let you finish your thought first. Then we work on grammar, pronunciation, and better phrasing after.”<br><br><strong>18–24s</strong> — Student confidently answers a mock interview question or presents to a small group.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> fluency comes from speaking—not staying silent<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “That’s how you build real confidence: safe practice, real conversations, repeat.”<br><br><strong>24–27s</strong> — Casual selfie-style end frame with students chatting in the background.<br><strong>On-screen:</strong> DM “SPEAK” to try a session<br><strong>Voiceover:</strong> “If speaking English makes you overthink everything, come practice with us.”`]],
      ['Soléa Fashion Co.', [`<strong>If your blazer survives ONE meeting pero hindi one wash… that’s not quiet luxury. That’s a scam with shoulder pads. 😭</strong><br><br>You’re telling me ang ganda sa website, very <em>clean girl, CEO, she has her life together</em>… tapos pagdating sa actual fabric, manipis, madaling gusutin, and after a few washes parang nakipaghiwalay na sa original shape niya?<br><br>Ubeee. No.<br><br>Being a minimalist doesn’t mean owning less just for the aesthetic. It means choosing pieces na paulit-ulit mong maisusuot because the fabric feels good, the tailoring actually holds, and hindi mo kailangang bumili ulit next month dahil nag-give up na yung tahi.<br><br>That’s the mindset behind Soléa Fashion Co.—timeless essentials that can take you from a serious 9AM presentation to a Friday dinner without looking like you changed personalities halfway through the day.<br><br>Because babe, your wardrobe should be giving <strong>cost per wear</strong>, not <em>cost per disappointment</em>. Period.<br><br>If you’ve been slowly breaking up with fast fashion, tell us: anong piece ang gusto mong i-upgrade first? ✨`, `<strong>Preheader:</strong> Your closet doesn’t need more. It needs better. Soléa essentials are 30% OFF for 48 hours.<br><br>There’s a very specific kind of delusion we need to address.<br><br>“It’s only ₱799.”<br><br>Cute.<br>Until you wear it three times.<br>Wash it twice.<br>And suddenly the neckline is somewhere in another barangay.<br><br>Now you need another top.<br>Then another pair of trousers.<br>Then another blazer because the first one started looking tired before <strong>you</strong> did.<br><br>So tell me:<br>Was it actually cheap?<br><br>Because buying the same mediocre thing four times is not exactly giving financial literacy.<br><br>At Soléa Fashion Co., we’re much more interested in the pieces you keep reaching for.<br><br>The trousers that work with almost everything.<br>The beautifully cut top that makes getting dressed suspiciously easy.<br>The neutral blazer that can handle Monday’s client presentation and Saturday’s brunch without screaming, <strong>“corporate uniform.”</strong><br><br>Less clutter.<br>More intention.<br>Better cost per wear.<br><br>And for the next <strong>48 hours</strong>, our <strong>Essential Edit is 30% OFF.</strong><br><br>We’re also giving qualifying flash-sale orders <strong>complimentary nationwide shipping.</strong><br><br>Consider this your excuse to finally replace the pieces in your closet that are technically still wearable…<br>but spiritually finished.<br><br><strong>[See the Soléa Essential Edit and secure your 30% flash-sale price here]</strong><br><br>Choose the pieces you can style again.<br>And again.<br>And again.<br><br>Because looking polished shouldn’t require owning 63 mediocre tops.<br><br>— <strong>Soléa Fashion Co.</strong><br><br><strong>P.S.</strong> The offer disappears after 48 hours and applies to qualifying Essential Edit pieces while stocks last. If you’ve had something sitting in your cart for two weeks, babe, at this point you two are basically dating.`, `If your “minimalist” top looks expensive online but turns into a sad, shapeless rag after one wash… that’s not quiet luxury. That’s just fast fashion in a beige color palette.<br><br><strong>5 tips to spot clothes that will actually last beyond one season</strong><br><br><strong>1. Check the fabric:</strong> Look for breathable, durable materials—not thin blends that feel plasticky.<br><br><strong>2. Inspect the seams:</strong> Clean, even stitching usually tells you more than the brand tag ever will.<br><br><strong>3. Look at the shape:</strong> Good tailoring should hold its structure even when it’s not styled on a model.<br><br><strong>4. Think in outfits:</strong> If you can wear it to work, dinner, and brunch, it’s already earning its place.<br><br><strong>5. Choose fewer, better pieces:</strong> One well-made staple beats replacing three cheap ones every few months.<br><br>Because babe, “less is more” only works when the <em>less</em> is actually good.<br><br>Save this before your next wardrobe checkout.`, `Can we stop pretending something is “premium” just because the product photo looks expensive?<br><br>Because if the fabric is paper-thin, the seams start fraying, and the whole thing loses its shape after one wash… babe, we were scammed by good lighting.<br><br>Soléa Fashion Co. is for the girls who would rather own fewer pieces that actually work hard in their wardrobe.<br><br>Think flattering tailoring, better fabrics, neutral colors, and pieces you can wear to a Monday meeting, Friday dinner, and Sunday brunch without looking like you repeated the same outfit.<br><br>Because buying less only works when you’re buying better.<br><br>Save this before your next closet clean-out. ✨`]],
    ];
    const categories = ['Ad Copy', 'Email', 'Tips', 'Short Video Script'];
    const body = oldGrid.querySelector('.copywriting-body');
    copyRows.forEach(function (row) {
